    "objective": "This project aimed to investigate how subconscious learning influences employee capabilities and development in rapidly evolving knowledge-based sectors. The research sought to address the gap between formal training methods and the actual learning experiences of employees.",
    "context": "The backdrop for this research includes the increasing challenges faced by knowledge-based industries, where formal training often fails to keep pace with technological advancements and evolving job demands. The project highlights the necessity for innovative training approaches that align with the dynamic nature of the workplace.",
    "approach": "The study employed the Subconscious Adaptive Learning Theory (SALT) as a framework to analyse learning processes in workplace settings. Methodologically, it included experiments and simulations to gather data on participant and agent results, followed by comprehensive data analysis.",
    "result": "The findings revealed that subconscious learning significantly enhances employee performance and adaptability, with specific data indicating improved engagement and retention rates. Recommendations included integrating SALT principles into formal training programmes to better align with employee learning behaviours.",
